{:edb/db-before-t 1187 :edb/db-after-t 1188 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534500 50 #inst "2026-10-07T09:20:39.281Z" 13194139534500 true] [17592186157238 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292089 13194139534500 true] [17592186157238 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292096 13194139534500 true] [17592186157238 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292117 13194139534500 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292103 13194139534500 true] [17592186157239 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292110 13194139534500 true] [17592186292089 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292090 13194139534500 true] [17592186292089 1089 "q-106462" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292089 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534500 true] [17592186292089 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/assets/6cd9c6a97d450761c01a9adb723985acbf4e5dc91e9877d7bd46c95db66d8c30.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292089 1113 #uuid "914c8844-0878-5387-a79a-b5ca32d2ccb2" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292089 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(3,1),$ and passes through the point $(-5,-7).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(3,1),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-3=p{t}^{2},\\,y-1=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,-7),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=-7$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-8=p{t}^{2} \\\\ -8=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =2pt \\\\ -4 & =pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{4}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =p{(-\\frac{4}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -8 & =p\\cdot \\frac{16}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -8 & =\\frac{16}{p} \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-3=(-2){t}^{2},\\,y-1=2(-2)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-3=-2{t}^{2},\\,y-1=-4t.\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292091 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292092 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292093 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292094 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292095 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1041 "selection" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292095 13194139534500 true] [17592186292090 1110 #uuid "b6b11901-df19-53f7-b179-442583776fda" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292091 1034 "x-3=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-1=-2t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292091 1111 #uuid "2d7da551-fc32-5399-967a-ca52f4de957a" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292092 1034 "x+3=-2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-4t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292092 1111 #uuid "d11c9e26-adff-5a42-bbcb-d4dc4a59cb34" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292093 1034 "x+3=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-1=-2t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292093 1111 #uuid "91b18fc2-d4f8-576c-95ba-ab19794784eb" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292094 1034 "x-3=-4t,\\,\\,y-1=-2{t}^{2}" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292094 1111 #uuid "4a538e83-fa76-5561-b11d-5d460fa79700" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292095 1034 "x-3=-2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-1=-4t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292095 1111 #uuid "00fe46db-a3d4-5b1b-a9b8-b17856c473cd" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292096 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292097 13194139534500 true] [17592186292096 1089 "q-106464" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292096 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534500 true] [17592186292096 1100 "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y-5)^{2}=2(x-2)?$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292096 1113 #uuid "b103e245-fa8b-566e-aedb-314d0caff13b" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292096 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(2,5).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx-2=p{t}^{2},\\,y-5=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =2(x-2) \\\\ 4p(x-2) & =2(x-2) \\\\ 4p & =2 \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-2=(\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\\,y-5=2(\\frac{1}{2})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y-5=t.\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292098 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292099 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292100 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292101 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292102 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1041 "selection" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292098 13194139534500 true] [17592186292097 1110 #uuid "1c1f251a-b759-512b-aeed-c7833b5ff71d" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292098 1034 "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-5=t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292098 1111 #uuid "f14d5ba4-85b6-520a-8734-6e7f0a153e0c" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292099 1034 "x-5=t,\\,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292099 1111 #uuid "2ca0e2ed-49f6-5181-9312-902ef85eb1e7" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292100 1034 "x-5=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-2=t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292100 1111 #uuid "bcc7d760-1a3e-55dd-8314-3c9b3f135582" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292101 1034 "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-5=2t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292101 1111 #uuid "af9dc71d-e91f-5d2b-bf3e-298a5b0c44bd" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292102 1034 "x+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292102 1111 #uuid "42a1e879-dc0a-5af0-be45-86a3eb7cbace" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292103 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292104 13194139534500 true] [17592186292103 1089 "q-106502" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292103 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534500 true] [17592186292103 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-2=-4t,\\,y-5=-2{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292103 1113 #uuid "2830887f-a29d-5706-9c2e-a6b72884e503" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292103 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x-2}{4},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{y-5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{x-2}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{y-5}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16} & =-\\frac{y-5}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-8(y-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292105 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292106 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292107 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292108 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292109 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1041 "selection" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292108 13194139534500 true] [17592186292104 1110 #uuid "0a00b481-bf85-58c8-b8ac-4381399f3886" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292105 1034 "(x-5)^{2}=-8(y-2)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292105 1111 #uuid "0ee9711b-2f58-5f63-8f70-bbcc2182287d" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292106 1034 "(y-5)^{2}=8(x-2)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292106 1111 #uuid "c6416754-c8d9-5f89-8385-0eb9c969c480" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292107 1034 "(y-5)^{2}=-8(x-2)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292107 1111 #uuid "1bcd83f9-d129-5bd3-b4b3-a0cb6de23969" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292108 1034 "(x-2)^{2}=-8(y-5)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292108 1111 #uuid "80ceae45-28dc-5749-a076-5b46dd832dfc" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292109 1034 "(x-2)^{2}=8(y-5)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292109 1111 #uuid "a4169520-377a-597f-a07d-944f9951066d" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292110 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292111 13194139534500 true] [17592186292110 1089 "q-106505" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292110 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534500 true] [17592186292110 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+3=-3{t}^{2},\\,y+5=-6t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292110 1113 #uuid "ab709b7e-f8e8-536b-98e9-55355fc9d0f8" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292110 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-\\frac{x+3}{3},\\,t=-\\frac{y+5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{y+5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{x+3}{3}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{36} & =-\\frac{x+3}{3} \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =36\\cdot (-\\frac{x+3}{3}) \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =-12(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292112 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292113 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292114 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292115 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292116 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1041 "selection" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292116 13194139534500 true] [17592186292111 1110 #uuid "939526f5-0c71-5b74-a2ec-e64d1ce8ae51" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292112 1034 "{(x+3)}^{2}=-12(y+5)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292112 1111 #uuid "000dd323-6f04-5cec-a785-91a41d441f4b" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292113 1034 "{(y+3)}^{2}=12(x+5)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292113 1111 #uuid "80c3cf99-360b-5fd9-8505-c77c356acc5e" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292114 1034 "{(y+3)}^{2}=-12(x+5)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292114 1111 #uuid "1fe977a6-1e95-5670-88c9-b8f8e26ea865" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292115 1034 "{(y+5)}^{2}=12(x+3)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292115 1111 #uuid "979a020e-cc11-5b0f-9858-3f280bc4d491" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292116 1034 "{(y+5)}^{2}=-12(x+3)" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292116 1111 #uuid "e827622c-fe4e-5291-8470-3ed13a485a1e" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292118 13194139534500 true] [17592186292117 1089 "q-84841" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534500 true] [17592186292117 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/assets/46929b27eb98506479401e2b78ea18fac539a11dcda4ecfb7b90c700dec61fdb.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292117 1113 #uuid "d6c249f9-5323-50ab-85ea-ed85b8d52bcf" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292117 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(1,-3),$ and passes through the point $(2,-4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(1,-3),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx-1=p{t}^{2},\\,y+3=2pt.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(2,-4),$ we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=-4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=p{t}^{2} \\\\ -1=2pt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =p{(-\\frac{1}{2p})}^{2} \\\\ 1 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{4{p}^{2}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{4p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-1=(\\frac{1}{4}){t}^{2},\\,y+3=2(\\frac{1}{4})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-1=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y+3=\\frac{1}{2}t.\n$$" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292119 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292120 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292121 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292122 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292123 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1041 "selection" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292121 13194139534500 true] [17592186292118 1110 #uuid "602ca50b-00fe-58a3-a0ee-5b438766a7d1" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292119 1034 "x+1=4{t}^{2},\\,y-3=8t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292119 1111 #uuid "7efb3891-6e6a-53b3-aaf7-4b0680a01652" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292120 1034 "x-1=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y+3=\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292120 1111 #uuid "87d33133-0d2e-5b1d-895b-a1d67b41d510" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292121 1034 "x-1=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y+3=\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292121 1111 #uuid "572b9ba6-caa0-5b35-b5ba-61c5fb837586" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292122 1034 "x-1=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y+3=\\frac{1}{8}t" 13194139534500 true] [17592186292122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534500 true] [17592186292122 1111 #uuid "df5ee550-c07e-505a-9f